<title>POLAND: Polish min T-bill prices inch down at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish min T-bill prices inch down at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 820 million zlotys against a one billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 656 million zlotys worth of T-bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     95.26    90.87     ---     83.18</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.27)  (90.89)    ---    (83.19)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.33    90.91     ---     83.40</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.40)  (91.00)    ---    (83.25)</p>
<p>   offer		---     400.0    100.0     ---     500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     403.4     54.1     ---     362.7</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     380.4     54.1     ---     221.2</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     300.0    200.0     ---     500.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
